We don't have the right kind of medicine here.

15
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Oh, please. I can't die like this.

16
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:47,000
You go. To something. He'll die if you don't. Please, you go.

17
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Don't do it. Bye.

18
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:54,000
If I live, so does my magic. Including the part Shaoran took with my eye.

19
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Even if he only has half, it's still too much.

20
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
He'll be completely unstoppable.

21
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:12,000
You coward! What kind of man is willing to just lay down and die like that?

22
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
No! Let him go!

23
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
I'm sorry.

24
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Well, witch. Is there a way for us to keep this idiot from dying?

25
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:41,000
There is. However, the price might be higher than you're willing to pay.

26
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Almost all of the underground reservoirs disappeared.

27
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
It's because of the portal that brought me here.

28
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:53,000
No. It's because of me. It was shortly after we arrived.

29
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:57,000
I found myself drawn to the mysterious power that laid deep in the water.

30
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,000
There's something at the bottom.

31
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Some power that's incredibly strong.

32
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Subaru! Subaru!

33
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,000
No! Stay back or it's just gonna pull you in here too!

34
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:24,000
She was sleeping. I drew her underwater through her dreams.

35
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:31,000
So you see, even if everything that happened down there was indeed inevitable, in the end it's still my fault that it happened where and when it did.

36
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Whether it's your fault or someone else's, nothing will change the fact that the water is gone.

37
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Perhaps I'm wrong. You look as if you may have an idea.

38
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Yes. It's been quite a while.

39
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
It has indeed.

40
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,000
I have another wish to make, and now my wish is for water.

41
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Enough to fill the cistern here.

42
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:02,000
There will be a price. Just as there was the last time we spoke when I gave you the ability to cross dimensions.

43
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Yes, I understand.

44
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Karogane?

45
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Karogane?

46
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Listen.

47
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,000
First, you must ask me to fill the underground reservoir.

48
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:17,000
It's an exchange. To repay you for taking on his wish, Subaru will give you the means to save Fi's life.

49
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:21,000
He's a vampire. His blood is the only hope Fi has now.

50
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:28,000
A vampire's body heals much more quickly than any human's does. With that blood, Fi will be able to recover.

51
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:34,000
However, preventing Fi's death is your wish. He does not wish it for himself.

52
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:39,000
Which means, reviving him will be your responsibility.

53
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,000
What do I need to do?

54
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
From today forward, you must be his game.

55
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:48,000
When he takes Subaru's blood, you must mix some of your own with it.

56
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:53,000
That way, yours will be the only blood he can drink, and no one innocent will be hurt.

57
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Yuko, does that mean if anything happens to him, Fi will-

58
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
He'll die.

59
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Very well. I understand. I accept the price. Now, give me your blood.

60
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
No, stop it.

61
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Shut up! If you want to die so bad, I'll kill you later myself. But until then, you're going to live.

62
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,000
I'll do it.

63
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,000
But Kamui...

64
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
I won't ever let someone else drink Subaru's blood again.

65
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Hold your arm out.

66
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Grab him tightly. His body is changing. It will be very painful.

67
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:55,000
We should go. I don't think we need to worry about them running away.

68
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Take the princess out of here!

69
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:04,000
What will happen to his left eye?

70
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:10,000
His eye was taken from him before ever becoming a vampire. It's too far gone now to grow back.

71
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Also, vampires are not immortal, despite what the legends may say.

72
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Vampires may not live forever, but they are much sturdier than humans, and they age quite a bit more slowly.

73
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:27,000
These two are purebred with considerable powers. Once his body's makeup has changed, Fi will heal as they do.

74
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Fi's lifespan won't change much. Magicians live longer than ordinary humans, just as vampires do.

75
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Fi's actually lived several times longer than you already.

76
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:41,000
You agreed to become his game without even understanding what it meant?

77
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:45,000
I had no choice. If we'd waited any longer to do something, he'd be dead now.

78
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Here's the deal. I don't always understand what the witch is planning, but she's the one that Cream Puffs sought out for help.

79
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
That thing trusts her. And after all this time, I trust it.

80
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
Do you, really?

81
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Fi!

82
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Fi!

83
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Fi!

84
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,000
Fi!

85
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,000
Fi!

86
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Fi!

87
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Fi!

88
