Flux!

89
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:25,000
There's still some questions that I want answered. But first, we'll see about that reservoir.

90
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
It's the guys from the tower!

91
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Oh, excuse me!

92
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,000
靴!

93
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:40,000
So there are two of you now, Kamui. Where's he from?

94
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Sakura's feather! But how? Mokuna should have sensed it coming closer!

95
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
I took steps so that wouldn't happen.

96
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
What are you talking about?

97
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:53,000
I had to keep it safe. And this feather can protect anything in its vicinity.

98
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Thanks to this little beauty, the tower didn't crumble even after years of acid rain.

99
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Of course, you already know that. It was the same for City Hall, right?

100
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Except, yours has disappeared, hasn't it?

101
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Why do you think that, Fuma?

102
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:11,000
You have a Dreamseer among your people, one who can predict the future.

103
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
We have a Priestess as well, with similar abilities.

104
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Even if that's true, why would you remove the feather from its place in the tower and bring it here?

105
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:23,000
You'd like to make a deal. We're offering this feather as a replacement.

106
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
And in return?

107
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:29,000
In return, you allow the people from the tower to come live here in City Hall.

108
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:33,000
We don't have much water left in our cistern. It won't hold out for long.

109
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:37,000
You have water, but you don't have a feather to protect it.

110
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:42,000
It's simple. You provide the water, we provide the feather. Both sides benefit.

111
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:47,000
There's plenty of room here for everyone to live comfortably. All we have to do is stop fighting and help each other.

112
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,000
What do you say?

113
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:52,000
The decision shouldn't be mine. I won't be staying here much longer.

114
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,000
Is that so?

115
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,000
You never mentioned this, Kamui. You're leaving Tokyo?

116
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Yes.

117
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:02,000
If that's the case, we won't stand a chance of defeating the guys from the tower.

118
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
You can say that again.

119
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Looks like we have to accept the deal.

120
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:12,000
But that belongs to Sakura! You can't keep it! It's Sakura's and it's really important!

121
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:18,000
We've been on a journey to find it for a very long time, and we lost a friend along the way. So you just can't!

122
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
Wait.

123
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
Sakura!

124
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,000
If this concerns the feather, please listen to me.

125
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Open the containers now.

126
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Whoa!

127
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Those things look too small to hold this much water!

128
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Right now, this water is pure. I've seen to it that it contains none of the dangerous contaminants that have affected the rest of the water on your world.

129
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:51,000
The protection is temporary. If you aren't careful, it too will become polluted.

130
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Before this water runs out, you must find a way to heal your world.

131
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:02,000
I still don't understand how you got all that water into this little thing.

132
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:06,000
You guys have some secrets, too. And what kind of container did you have that feather in, anyway?

133
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Whatever it is, it didn't come from this world. This place has no indigenous power. So why would there be anything here that's designed to suppress magic?

134
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:20,000
You're right. I didn't find it here at all. I brought it with me from another dimension about four years ago.

135
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Good afternoon, Yuko. I haven't had a method of contacting you since I reached this world, but I hope you've been doing well.

136
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
You picked up that container on one of those little trips of yours, didn't you?

137
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Yeah. That is my job, after all. I'm a hunter of sorts, and I seek things across different worlds.

138
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Most of the time I work for clients who are searching for things of great value, but sometimes I work for myself.

139
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:50,000
I believe you two have already met my brother. He and I call ourselves hunters, though we hunt different things.

140
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:57,000
It's a pleasure to meet you. You are the vampire Subaru, right? Thank you for taking care of Seishiro, my brother.

141
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:07,000
What? You're relating to the man who's been hunting us?

142
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:14,000
As I said, my brother and I are different. Anyway, he isn't here now. Why don't you and I take care of our business before he shows up?

143
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:17,000
So, Yuko, what's the price?

144
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Are you ready to hear it?

145
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
I am.

146
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Whatever it is, I...

147
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
No, I'll do it!

148
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Sakura!

149
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:32,000
If there's a price to pay, I'll pay it this time. If you wouldn't mind, please fill me in on what happened while I was sleeping.

150
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Yuko, you can't ask that! The rain in this world burns! And there are big monsters everywhere! It's too dangerous!

151
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:50,000
It's the only way. Sakura must retrieve what I asked for without any help. That is the price.

152
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Alright. Ready to go?

153
00:12:53,000 --> 00:13:10,000
I'm so sorry. You were hurt because I asked you to stop. Rest. I hope you'll heal up soon. You get some good rest too, okay, Mokuna? I know Fi is in good hands with you here.

154
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:20,000
There's nothing I could say that would change your mind, I guess. I get it then. In that case, I'll just wish you good luck. We'll be waiting here when you get back.

155
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Thanks.

156
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Something wrong?

157
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
How is Seishiro?

158
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Well, let's see. He ages more slowly, of course, and he's got more energy than I've ever seen before. He's very intent on catching up with you two. He's a hunter. He won't stop until he has.

159
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
We aren't gonna let that happen.

160
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
We'll see about that.

161
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Come on, let's all try to keep our cool. We've got other things to worry about now.

162
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Sha'ron.

163
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:35,100
Charon, even your name's the same as his.

164
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:36,100
Yeah.

165
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:39,740
You were locked up for a really long time.

166
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:41,320
It must have been lonely.

167
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,640
Not really. I saw everything.

168
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:45,740
I was watching through his eyes the whole time.

169
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:46,880
I was always there.

170
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:49,160
That must have been even harder for you.

171
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:52,240
All you could do is watch while Moken and the others had fun.

172
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:57,040
It was difficult and scary sometimes, but we still loved being together.

173
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:58,560
I'm so sorry.

174
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:03,140
You must have wanted to come along too, didn't you?

175
00:15:05,380 --> 00:15:06,680
I guess I did.

176
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:52,220
I guess I did.

177
00:15:52,240 --> 00:16:03,240
Good morning, Kurokane.

178
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:07,780
Don't move.

179
00:16:07,780 --> 00:16:27,780
Bye.

180
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:29,780
Bye.

181
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:31,780
Bye.

182
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:40,980
Yes, I'm sorry if you were worried about me.

183
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:44,720
Mokuna, I'd like you to take a little nap, but keep the transmission going.

184
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:46,980
I want to speak with Fi alone.

185
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:51,340
Have you talked to him?

186
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:54,860
I told him good morning. It wasn't a long conversation.

187
00:16:55,540 --> 00:16:58,140
After everything that's happened, is that all you have to say?

188
00:16:58,140 --> 00:17:03,200
You know, when we first met, I was going to call him by his full name, just like I did everyone else.

189
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:07,700
But he got so angry when I called him Kurupu that I couldn't help myself.

190
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:12,280
It was something new. I'd never called anyone by a nickname before.

191
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:19,740
It was so fun that I didn't realize I was beginning to cross the line I had drawn for myself.

192
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:25,640
But now I have a chance to fix that. I can never forgive him for saving my life.

193
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:29,920
If I did, we'd just become close again.

194
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:38,760
Haven't you figured it out yet?

195
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:42,720
Your fears are their fears. Your pain is their pain.

196
00:17:44,260 --> 00:17:47,100
How's Sakura? Is she still sleeping upstairs?

197
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:49,840
No. She's gone.

198
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:55,740
Thank you.

199
00:17:57,360 --> 00:18:00,240
It's not like wearing that crest is something you chose to do.

200
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:04,560
I know. But I'm sure you'd rather not look at it all the same.

201
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:08,980
The witch told me you'd been held captive all this time, by the man whose crest that is.

202
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:09,860
Yes.

203
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:14,660
I'm sorry. I can't help you.

204
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:17,220
I don't know where he is or how to find him.

205
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:20,860
Even if I did know, I don't have the power to cross dimensions.

206
00:18:21,340 --> 00:18:22,580
So I couldn't take you to it.

207
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,760
Again, I don't blame you for that.

208
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:40,440
I don't mind, wait for it.

209
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:45,940
I don't blame you for that.

210
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:46,180
No problem.

211
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:47,660
No problem.

212
00:18:47,660 --> 00:19:15,140
It won't end here.

213
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:20,980
There will be more times when I have to put others in danger, when I'll have to fight or steal to get what I need.

214
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:24,660
I'm sure I'll pay for it in the end, but I accept that.

215
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:26,280
It won't stop me.

216
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:33,960
Because, no matter what, I'll keep going for your sake, and I'm going to get your soul back for you.

217
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:35,080
Shelra.

218
00:19:42,180 --> 00:19:44,820
How? How could you ever do that?

219
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:47,140
How could you let Sakura go out there alone?

220
00:19:47,140 --> 00:20:08,740
The compass is broken.

221
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:20,880
hold on bye you're going out after the princess is that it why do you care if i am don't go

222
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:29,920
wait for her here with us she might be injured for all we know she's lying out there somewhere

223
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:34,600
utterly helpless if she doesn't come back i'll never forgive myself for not looking

224
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:39,760
for not doing something the princess knew how dangerous it was when she decided to go

225
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:45,240
if she really understood that then why did she go at all

226
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:52,220
i'm almost there except there's no trail here to follow anymore

227
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:13,080
who are you she made her choice and i believed her when she promised to come back to those who

228
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:15,440
were waiting for her so i will wait

229
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:18,880
well i won't

230
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:27,760
don't try to stop her or i promise i'll fight you

231
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:36,260
don't go if you follow her she'll know that you didn't have any faith in her promise

232
00:21:36,260 --> 00:21:38,860
that will wound her more than any physical injury

